cff-version: 1.3.0
message: "If you use AbScout, PanelScout or Methods Writer, please cite them as below."
title: "AbScout, PanelScout and Methods Writer: panel design and methods reporting tools for spatial biology"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pathare
    given-names: Suyog
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8856-3796"
version: 1.3.0
date-released: 2026-11-22
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/suyogpathare/panel-design-tools"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24326636
url: "https://suyogpathare.com/#tools"
abstract: >-
  AbScout searches the Antibody Registry for a target, ranks antibodies by
  use in HuBMAP Organ Mapping Antibody Panels, citations and reactivity, and
  builds multiplex imaging panels with host, fluorophore, knockout-validation
  (YCharOS) and spectral bleed-through (FPbase) checks, informed by Human
  Protein Atlas tissue RNA levels, and keeps a per-antibody validation
  record under the five IWGAV strategies. PanelScout reports how much of a gene list
  each imaging spatial transcriptomics panel covers, from panel files the user
  loads from the vendors, resolving aliases through HGNC and MGI. Methods Writer drafts the
  methods section and a channel-level metadata table for a multiplex tissue
  imaging study, following the MITI reporting guidelines, from what the user
  enters.
keywords:
  - spatial biology
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - multiplex immunofluorescence
  - antibody validation
  - panel design
  - knockout validation
  - MITI
  - reporting guidelines
